### Format ###

# Parameters:
#
# audience: the target audience (backed by checkin groups), such as "droidfood".
# branch: the branch name, such as "git_oc-release".
# build_prefix: the prefix for the release candidate id, such as "OR" for short
#     build id, or "APAA" for long build id.
# release_candidate_id: the release candidate id of a build, such as "ORF41B"
#     for short build id, or "APAA.170123.001" for long build id.

# BRANCH <build_prefix> <branch>
#
#     Specifies what branch to use for a given build prefix.

# OTA <audience> <device_model> <build_config,...>
#
#     Specifies one or more named builds to be sent to devices in the audience
#     and with the specified device_model that are already running a build from
#     the same series. For instance if you say "DMD64,ERD15", then DMD64 will be
#     sent to any device already running a DM build, and ERD15 to any device
#     running an ER build. Devices running other builds will not get an OTA.
#
#     Optionally, the build series prequisite can be explictly specified using
#     "<build_prefix>=release_candidate_id" syntax. For example, to send ORF41B
#     to devices running a N2 build, state "N2=ORF41B".
#
#     A build name can be replaced with "LATEST($build_prefix)" or
#     "LATEST_WEEKDAY($build_prefix)" to mean "the latest green (weekday) build
#     for the target on that branch".



